# Kubelet & Worker Node Diagnostics Guide

Worker node failures and `NotReady` states in the CKA exam typically stem from kubelet service failure, container runtime issues, or invalid configuration parameters.

---

## Official Exam References & Quick Lookups

### Permitted Exam Documentation

- **Worker Node Troubleshooting**: [Troubleshoot Clusters](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/debug/debug-cluster/#troubleshooting-worker-nodes) `[EXAM ALLOWED]`
- **kubelet Configuration**: [kubelet Configuration](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/config-api/kubelet-config.v1beta1/) `[EXAM ALLOWED]`

### In-Exam Search Keywords

- `"troubleshoot worker nodes"`
- `"kubelet configuration"`

### Terminal Fast Lookups (`systemctl` / `journalctl`)

```bash
sudo systemctl status kubelet
sudo journalctl -u kubelet -e --no-pager
sudo systemctl restart kubelet
```

